; fault_condcode.kasm -- a predicate prefix naming a condition that does not
; exist.
;
; Only five of `arg2`'s 32 values are assigned condition codes (spec 7, codes
; 27..31). The other 27 make the prefix illegal, and the two machines used to
; disagree about that in the most confusing possible way: the RTL faulted,
; while the emulator decided the code point was not a prefix at all and decoded
; it as a main opcode. Not a wrong answer to the question -- a different
; instruction, executed.
;
; The spec has carried this as `[N]` with a note that the emulator did not
; implement it. Now both do, and this program is what keeps them together.
;
; Written as a `.word` because the assembler only emits the five real
; conditions; there is no way to ask it for this.

        .org    0

        .word   0x7c20          ; XCP r1, <unassigned condition code>
        halt
